			"notes": "**Industrial Legacy**\n**Version:** Alpha 0.1.6\n\n**Dev Blog**\n\n⛏ **Resources and Blocks**\n• Added **Aluminum Ore** and **Lithium Ore**, along with their derivatives. For now, they do **not generate naturally**.\n• Added **Silver Ore**, which now generates **in large amounts beneath mountain biomes**.\n• Added **deepslate variants** for all ore types.\n• Regular ores no longer generate in the **deepslate zone**.\n• Increased the generation rate of **Lead, Tin, and Uranium** veins.\n• Added **Iron, Bronze, Steel, and Fuel Rods**.\n• Added an **Iron Fence**.\n• Added a **Steel Ingot**.\n\n🔌⚡ **Electronics**\n• **Uninsulated Copper Cables** now **oxidize**. They can be **scraped with an axe**, just like other copper-based blocks. The higher the oxidation level, the greater the **energy loss per cable block**.\n• Cables can now be **insulated with Rubber**.\n• Added **LV, MV, HV, and SHV Transformers**.\n• Added the **Metal Former** and its recipes.\n• Energy display has been updated to match the **IC2 style**.\n• Energy net logic has been brought closer to the behavior of the **original IC2**.\n\n🪛 **Fixes**\n• Fixed incorrect **energy net invalidation**.\n• Fixed energy net issues during **chunk loading and unloading**.\n• Fixed **redstone mode** for **CESU** and **MFE**.\n• Fixed a UI issue where **Generator, BatBox, CESU, and MFE** were missing background darkening.\n• Fixed a **mixin conflict** involving **Nano Armor**.\n• Fixed an issue with **energy storage placement** that caused them to be placeable only horizontally.\n• Changed the default cable color from **white to black** to better match the **IC2 canon**.\n• Fixed a bug that allowed placing a cable where another cable already existed.\n• Fixed the missing **Compressor recipe**.\n• Improved the stability of the **Compressor crafting system**."
		},
